# Universal Design System — CWP Detailers

When creating, editing, styling, modernizing, or auditing any user interface in the CWP Detailers ecosystem:

1. **Canonical Skill**: Always consult `.cursor/skills/universal-design-system/SKILL.md` (and `.agents/skills/universal-design-system/SKILL.md`).
2. **Tokens Over Ad-Hoc Values**: Never introduce arbitrary hex codes, random paddings, unmeasured shadows, or ad-hoc typography. Consume semantic tokens from `@/features/admin-ds`, `@/features/staff-ds`, `@/features/customer-ds`, or the shared CWP Universal Design System foundation.
3. **Material Design 3 Iconography (Mandatory)**: Follow official Material Design 3 icon standards (https://m3.material.io/styles/icons/overview). Use consistent Material Symbols, stroke weights, optical alignments, and sizes. No emoji as UI icons.
4. **Role-Specific Design Adaptation**:
   - **Admin Application**: High information density, clear operational hierarchy, data tables, quick triage.
   - **Staff Application**: High-contrast outdoor readability, minimum 44px–48px touch targets, bilingual Hindi-first, offline resilience.
   - **Customer Application**: Clean white surfaces, subtle micro-shadows, 16:10 visual cards, frictionless booking.
5. **Living PRD Synchronization**: Update `docs/product/CWP_NOIDA_MULTI_CITY_PRD.md` in the same work cycle.
